  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "Recent releases package established genomic, CRISPR screen, and CLIP analysis steps into faster, more automated, locally runnable tools.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is re-engineering of established analysis steps for speed, automation, and usability rather than introducing new analysis paradigms. deepTools4 rewrites core functions of its genomic sequencing suite, reporting benchmarked speed-ups and updated visualization. MAUDE-Py reimplements the MAUDE probabilistic framework in Python for sorting-based pooled CRISPR screens, adding automated baselines and null sampling. CLIPittyClip packages CLIP sequencing analysis as a local single-command pipeline from raw FASTQ to peak matrices and crosslink sites, with a 27-fold faster Python crosslink step. Other items are less directly tool-oriented: bsseq presents a read-based likelihood framework for identifying sample-specific CpG loci in Nanopore and PacBio long-read data, and MethMarkerDB 2.0 expands a cancer DNA methylation biomarker database with CpG-level and functional analysis modules.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
